 # Therapy_Schedule
+
+## Weekly Minutes, Gap-Fill & AI Scheduling Assistant
+
+Three additions on top of the existing board:
+
+### 1. Per-patient weekly minute tracker
+Each patient's "week" (for the 900-minute, or custom, target) starts on their
+own admission day-of-week — not a shared Monday calendar week. Two patients
+admitted on different days have different week boundaries. See
+`shared/weekUtils.ts` for the math and `Weekly Minutes` panel (header button)
+for the UI: progress per patient, minutes remaining, days left in their week.
+
+### 2. Gap-fill suggestions
+For any patient under target, click "Suggest open slots" in the Weekly
+Minutes panel. The engine (`server/scheduling.ts`) scans the rest of their
+week for grid slots where both the patient and a therapist (preferring their
+own team) are free, and proposes 30/45/60-minute blocks to close the gap.
+Each suggestion has an "Add" button that creates a real session.
+
+### 3. Ask the Scheduler (free, self-hosted AI)
+The "Ask Scheduler" header button opens a chat that answers questions like
+"who's at risk this week" or "who can cover Room 214's gap" using a **free,
+local** model via [Ollama](https://ollama.com) — no API key, no cloud spend.
+
+**Setup (one-time, on the machine running the server):**
+```bash
+# 1. Install Ollama: https://ollama.com/download
+# 2. Pull a model (this one is small/fast; swap for a bigger one if you have the RAM)
+ollama pull llama3.1
+# 3. Start the Ollama server (leave this running)
+ollama serve
+```
+Then start the app as usual (`npm run dev`). By default it talks to Ollama at
+`http://localhost:11434` using the `llama3.1` model. Override with env vars if
+needed:
+```
+OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
+OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.1
+```
+If Ollama isn't reachable, the assistant still replies — it falls back to
